# Force LF regardless of the checking-out platform's autocrlf setting.
# Without this, files written/edited on Windows (core.autocrlf=true here)
# risk ending up with CRLF line endings — harmless for most files, but a
# CRLF shebang line breaks a shell script with "bad interpreter" on the
# actual Linux VPS/CI runner these files are meant to run on.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
